# Frontend Conventions

- Server Components by default; Client Components only where
  interactivity is required.
- No `any`. Co-locate component types with the component.
- Keep components under ~200 lines.
- `needs_review` orders must be visually distinct, never a small badge.
- Every screen must implement loading, empty, error, and any
  domain-specific states the spec defines — not just the happy path.
- This UI is used by a non-technical end user (Dad) on the admin side,
  and by customers quickly on their phones on the order side. Favor
  obvious over clever.

